": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b60d1720de644f3770b581e4de5fccfe9534f7a43b88d4b4716354cc86179fbd","event_uuid":"4d68078b-d9fe-4a4c-8df7-f1dfb5f92262","position":{"commit_sha":"c19828109ff8c67819646304d3999af5b9ee2801","position":"1786305755393733001-4d68078b-d9fe-4a4c-8df7-f1dfb5f92262"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"REBAR-DEBUG PHASE 1 — confirmed root cause (correcting the original abort narrative)\n\nThe fixed `.cache.json.tmp` pathname is a real concurrency defect, but it does not make the immutable gate-snapshot fan-out abort: 16 barrier-synchronized real `reduce_ticket` calls produced 15 caught FileNotFoundError warnings, zero escaped exceptions, equal results, and a valid final cache. Repository logging was also proven non-throwing; only a deliberately rethrowing negative-control handler escaped.\n\nThe confirmed defect is more serious and broader: two reductions of different event generations open/truncate the same temp inode. One rename can expose that inode as `.cache.json` while another writer continues mutating it, splicing fields from independently valid `{dir_hash,state}` envelopes. A real reducer experiment appended an EDIT between eight old-generation and eight new-generation reductions. In 14 rounds it produced a final cache carrying the CURRENT generation hash but stale state (`authorship` remained signed=1/unsigned=0 instead of signed=1/unsigned=1). A subsequent normal `reduce_ticket` returned that wrong cached state while replay was replaced with a sentinel that would raise, proving a false cache hit. Thirty serialized control rounds produced zero false hits.\n\nRoot cause: `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:143` assigns every writer `cache_path + \".tmp\"`; `read_cache` validates the outer hash and attestation-kind parity but cannot detect ordinary fields spliced from another generation. This violates the function contract to atomically write one state envelope, the reducer-cache invalidation contract, and the event-sourced invariant that compiled state is deterministic replay. The original plan-review-abort explanation is rejected; the repaired ticket targets coherent atomic publication under concurrent, divergent writers.","timestamp":1786302639984111001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation update: refreshed origin/main and confirmed exact base 89128b2e09 before commit. Proven RCA is shared fixed-temp cache publication: overlapping file descriptors could mutate a current-hash envelope after rename. The repair uses fsutil.atomic_write unique temps, routes corrupt CREATE through canonical write_cache, and ignores private cache temp names recursively. Evidence: held-out oracle 5 passed; fixed-temp mutation produced 3 mechanism failures and restored GREEN; root/nested git-add plus module-size probes 6 passed; focused reducer suites 228 passed, 1 skipped; final combined gate 11 passed; lint, typecheck, and diff check pass; independent cross-review approved with no findings. Committed as c571bdde47 and uploaded as Gerrit change 1569. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before Submit. Ticket intentionally remains in_progress per operator directive.","timestamp":1786305755393733001}],"created_at":1786117812903549001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"07cdff04-2099-457b-9c99-b4119df4b80d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1e88-687f-45d1-435f"},{"link_uuid":"cccd11a6-a574-477e-a036-9f7d46229e38","relation":"blocks","target_id":"12b7-735f-e2fa-498a"},{"link_uuid":"137e2fa6-bcd8-4585-9ab8-463759f8a94a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"098e-19e1-4673-4598"}],"description":"# Concurrent reducer cache writers can publish a current hash with stale state\n\n## Context and authoritative intent\n\nThe reducer cache is a rebuildable optimization over deterministic event replay. `write_cache` promises an atomic cache publication, the cache invalidation tests require a newly added event to be reflected, and the original plan-review fan-out epic `sulky-pane-flag` requires concurrency without fidelity regression.\n\nThe report originally attributed a cap=12 plan-review abort to the `.cache.json.tmp` rename race. Phase-1 experiments rejected that fatality claim for immutable gate snapshots: redundant writers log caught warnings but do not escape or corrupt the equal result. The confirmed defect is reachable when concurrent reductions observe different event generations.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\nTwo reducer cache writers use the same fixed `.cache.json.tmp` artifact: `write_cache` in `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py` and corrupt-CREATE handling in `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`. Overlapping writers can hold file descriptors to the same inode; after one renames it into place, another can keep mutating the now-visible final file. Runtime proof through real `reduce_ticket` appended an EDIT between old-generation and new-generation reductions and produced a valid cache with the current hash but stale `authorship`. A subsequent normal reduction returned the stale cached state without replay. Serialized controls produced no false hits.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n1. Replace `write_cache` fixed-temp publication with the canonical `rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write`, preserving the surrounding best-effort OSError handling.\n2. Route the inline corrupt-CREATE cache publication in `process_create` through `write_cache`, so every reducer cache writer shares the isolated same-directory temp, atomic replace, cleanup, and failure policy.\n3. Extend the canonical tracker gitignore ensure-registry for `atomic_write` private cache temp names and pin that registry/staging contract.\n4. Add deterministic threaded reducer regressions through the real cache seam: capture coherent old/new states around a controlled event append, release at least eight writers, and assert the current-hash read equals a cache-bypassing replay oracle. Add an immutable-writer control and a corrupt-CREATE writer control so no fixed `.cache.json.tmp` writer remains.\n5. Run the focused reducer/cache and init/gitignore suites, then lint and typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Concurrent reductions of different event generations publish only complete coherent envelopes; a current-hash cache hit equals cache-bypassing deterministic replay.\n- [ ] At least eight concurrent reductions of one immutable ticket complete without `FileNotFoundError` cache-write warnings.\n- [ ] The normal and corrupt-CREATE cache paths both publish through the canonical `atomic_write` mechanism.\n- [ ] Publication failure cleanup leaves no private cache temp files.\n- [ ] Every private cache temp artifact shape is covered by the canonical tracker gitignore/ensure-registry contract.\n- [ ] A `git add -A` staging probe excludes every private cache temp artifact shape.\n- [ ] Cache publication failure is logged and does not prevent independently replayed ticket state from returning.\n- [ ] Focused reducer/cache and init/gitignore tests pass.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py","reason":"Publish cache envelopes through canonical atomic_write while preserving best-effort failure handling"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","reason":"Route corrupt-CREATE cache publication through the shared write_cache path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"Ensure canonical private cache temp artifacts are ignored in every tracker"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reducer_cache_concurrency_c1fd.py","reason":"Held-out threaded old/new-generation, identical-writer, and corrupt-CREATE cache oracles"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_cache_gitignored.py","reason":"Pin private cache temp artifact ignore and git add -A staging safety"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["blocks","12b7-735f-e2fa-498a"],["relates_to","098e-19e1-4673-4598"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"fecfaf3e-61df-4775-80cd-246a2b499767","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["concurrency","plan-review","cache"],"ticket_id":"c1fd-be12-44b7-4d31","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Concurrent reducer cache writers can publish a current hash with stale state","verify_commands":[{"command":"pytest -q tests/unit/test_reducer_cache_concurrency_c1fd.py","dd_id":"cache-concurrency","dd_text":"Concurrent current-hash cache hits equal cache-bypassing replay and identical writers do not race temp renames"},{"command":"pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_cache_gitignored.py","dd_id":"cache-ignore","dd_text":"Private cache temps are covered by the tracker ensure-registry and cannot be staged"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"quality","dd_text":"Repository lint and types remain clean"}]},"source_event_uuids":["25d356c6-9e6c-4795-91e3-1b68b4165dcc","07cdff04-2099-457b-9c99-b4119df4b80d","cccd11a6-a574-477e-a036-9f7d46229e38","167a44e7-ddc1-4880-99d4-504f1998657f","22c47547-bfdf-40e8-a742-ab14ff8b8350","59ac0972-f0d9-41b4-953a-dd29f476af6d","0f2db614-a72a-4f11-846b-a8986ed7d41b","30db2c53-d017-4eca-ba7d-1f4820f5ce58","4a4699c4-09e5-4a71-a63f-717a17ab3310","fc0490bf-c47e-4e37-9c4a-0785ffe633f5","09a350e1-98ff-44f3-a715-73781261603c","3479bea5-b5d6-4ed6-90ac-be8a5d1b40c9","fecfaf3e-61df-4775-80cd-246a2b499767","ca10cd83-9c66-41b7-9e3c-629f4034470d","4d68078b-d9fe-4a4c-8df7-f1dfb5f92262","137e2fa6-bcd8-4585-9ab8-463759f8a94a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786306059497121837,"uuid":"68b4f061-c4fa-4cae-9a09-84d398748917"}